// v0.3-M2 Phase 7 Round-3: recursive SM cancellation-no-leak fixture.
// TIMING DESIGN: countdown(n) sleeps 200ms per level. entrypoint waits 500ms
// before allowing shutdown (with YNZ_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS=50).
//
// Alloc accounting includes the entrypoint's own frame (alloc=1 from wrapper).
// Timeline from ynz_rt_init:
//   At   0ms: entrypoint frame alloc'd (alloc=1). countdown(3) spawned, root alloc'd (alloc=2).
//   At 200ms: countdown(3) wakes, allocates countdown(2) heap-box (alloc=3), polls countdown(2).
//             countdown(2) hits its 200ms sleep.
//   At 400ms: countdown(2) wakes, allocates countdown(1) heap-box (alloc=4), polls countdown(1).
//             countdown(1) hits its 200ms sleep.
//   At 500ms: entrypoint wakes, calls ynz_rt_shutdown(timeout=50ms).
//             countdown(1) is 100ms into its 200ms sleep — 4 heap-boxed frames are live.
//   At 550ms: Tokio's 50ms grace period expires. SpawnStateFnFuture is dropped.
//             SpawnStateFnFuture::Drop walks the recursion chain: frees countdown(1),
//             countdown(2), root. alloc=4, free=4 (no leak).
//   [countdown(1)'s natural sleep end would be at ~600ms — 50ms after the cancel fires.]
//
// YNZ_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS=50 (not 0): a 0ms timeout races between ynz_rt_shutdown reading
// the counters and the worker thread running Drop. 50ms gives Tokio time to join threads
// (ensuring Drop has run) while still cancelling before countdown(1) completes at ~600ms.
//
// Expected: alloc_count == free_count (no leak with chain walk).
// Negative control (YNZ_SKIP_RECURSION_DROP=1): alloc=4, free=2 (chain walk skipped,
// countdown(1) and countdown(2) leaked).
//
// The 3 recursion_cancellation* tests are serialized via a static Mutex in the
// test harness — no CPU contention can affect relative timing across these tests.

function countdown(n: int) -> nothing {
  if (n > 0) {
    wait sleep(200)
    countdown(n - 1)
  }
}

function entrypoint() -> nothing {
  background countdown(3)
  wait sleep(500)
  print(`done`)
}
